,"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":47,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I did the document stage for `pay-through-the-provider` in this session and wrote `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/document.md`. I committed nothing and ran no other stage. The only check I ran was `./gradlew spotlessCheck`, which passed.\n\n**Glossary** (`src/main/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/checkout/domain/glossary.md`, edited using the `ubiquitous-language` skill):\n- **New `PaymentResult` entry:** it defines the three outcomes, `SUCCEEDED`, `REFUSED` and `UNAVAILABLE` (authorized payment, refused payment, unavailable provider). It also covers the payment request and the payment stand-in.\n- **`PaymentProviderId`:** now names both ids. `provider` is used when `checkout.payment-provider.base-url` is set, and `mock` otherwise (judge finding 3).\n- **Payment failures entry:** now says the provider's reason is kept for logs and callers, and the payment page shows the customer its own fixed message (judge finding 2).\n\n**Other documents:**\n- **`PaymentInitiationFailedException.java`:** I changed only its JavaDoc, so it matches the glossary change. This is a comment in production code, but no code changed.\n- **`project/domain.md`:** the \"Payment Service Provider\" row now says the REST adapter is used when the address is configured and the stand-in otherwise. I used the `context-map` skill; the relationship and its pattern are unchanged.\n- **`project/product.md`:** \"a stand-in in the sample, unless a provider address is configured\".\n- **`README.md`:** the checkout file tree lists the new files, including the `infrastructure/` folder, which was missing from the tree before. \"Running the Application\" now shows how to point the shop at a real provider.\n- **`docs/architecture/package-structure.md`:** lists the new payment adapter files.\n- **`docs/architecture/context-map.md`:** I left it alone, because the build stage already regenerated it.\n\n**Not documented** (the reasons are in `document.md`):\n- `project/product.md` still lists \"Real payment\" as not part of the product. Whether to change that is a product decision for you.\n- `PaymentResult.failure(..)` always gives `REFUSED` (judge finding 1). Fixing that needs a code change, not a document edit.\n- The field names in the request and answer, and treating any unexpected answer as \"unavailable\", were assumptions in the plan. `project/tech.md` doesn't state them, and I left that file unchanged.","ttft_ms":4314,"type":"result","duration_ms":150017,"uuid":"180863a1-bc5e-4be4-9894-4215606b8d9e","ttft_stream_ms":3916,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":3917,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
